[Lemma lem:uit-raw-moments-particle of arXiv:2605.20697, 'Uniform-in-time propagation of chaos for \\ Second-Order Consensus-Based Optimization'] Let $p \geqslant 2$. Under (assumption:bounded of the paper), (assump:admissibility of the paper), and the stability conditions of (thm:exp-decay-centered-moments of the paper), there exists a finite constant $K_{\mathrm{raw}} > 0$ such that:
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbf{E} \left[ \sup_{t \geqslant 0} |X_t^j|^p \right] \leqslant K_{\mathrm{raw}} \quad \text{and} \quad \sup_{t \geqslant 0} \mathbf{E} \left[ |V_t^j|^p \right] \leqslant K_{\mathrm{raw}}.
    \end{equation}

[Theorem 59 (All-degree intrinsic primitive--Fock unitary) of arXiv:2608.12492, 'Weak Limits of Wiener Chaos: Primitive--Fock Classification and Hilbert--Stein Extraction'] The direct sum
\begin{equation}
 \mathbb U=\bigoplus_{q\ge1}\mathbb U_q

\end{equation}
is a unitary
\begin{equation}
 \mathbb U:
 \bigoplus_{q\ge1}
 \cW_q\left(\bigoplus_{s\le q}\cK_s\right)
 \xrightarrow{\ \simeq\ }
 \bigoplus_{q\ge1}\cH_q,
 \qquad P_{\le Q}\mathbb U=\mathbb U P_{\le Q}.

\end{equation}
It is an isometry at every level of the compact Hilbert scale for which the corresponding
weighted norm is finite.  Condition $\mathrm{QT}_2$ is used only to ensure that the represented
packet belongs to the grade-wise direct sum on the right-hand side.

