body:
[Lemma 16 of arXiv:2510.20492, 'Heterochromatic two-arm probabilities for metric graph Gaussian free fields'] For any $d\ge 3$, there exist $C,c>0$ such that for any $T>0$, $D\subset \widetilde{\mathbb{Z}}^d$ and $v,w\in \widetilde{\mathbb{Z}}^d\setminus D$ with $|v-w|\ge d$, 
	\begin{equation}
		\mathbb{P}\big( \widehat{\mathcal{L}}_{1/2}^{D,v}\ge T \mid  v\xleftrightarrow{(D)} w \big) \le Ce^{-cT}. 
	\end{equation}

