[Definition of arXiv:2608.10415, 'Continuous random variables'] An abstract operator algebra, or $C^*$-algebra, is a complex algebra $A$ having a norm $||.||$ and an involution $*$, subject to the following conditions:
\begin{enumerate}
\item $A$ is closed with respect to the norm.

\item We have $||aa^*||=||a||^2$, for any $a\in A$.
\end{enumerate}

[Lemma 13 (Thin boundary-layer volume) of arXiv:2607.19752, 'Weak Equilibrium Measures and Capacity--Hitting Identities\\ for the Hypoelliptic Third-Or'] Let $\Sigma\in\{\partial A,\partial B,\partial\calD\}$ and let
$K_1\subset\R^{3d}$ be compact.  There exist constants $a_0,b_0,C>0$ such that,
for $0<a\le a_0$ and $0<b\le b_0$,
\[
    \operatorname{Leb}\left\{
        y\in K_1:\dist(y,\Sigma)\le a,\ |r(y)|\le b
    \right\}
    \le C a b^d .
\]

