[Lemma 23 of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] Let $G = (V,E)$ be a finite graph with at least one cycle and distinct edge weights $\{\exp(-\beta \omega_e)\}_{e\in E}$. Then the quantity 
\begin{equation}
    g(\beta) =  \sum_{T \in \T(G)} \bP^{\omega}_{G, \beta}( \cT = T)^2
\end{equation}
is strictly increasing in $\beta$ and tends to one as $\beta \rightarrow \infty$.

