[Definition notation:BCset1 of arXiv:2511.15893, 'On a Class of Dynamical Poisson-Voronoi Tessellations'] For each $(R,\alpha)$ atom of  $\tilde{\Phi}$, let 

\begin{equation}
C_{(R,\alpha)}:=\left\{(t, f((R,\alpha), t)): t\in \mathbb{R}\right\}.

\end{equation} 

We call the infinite closed set $C_{(R,\alpha)}\subset\mathbb{H}^+$ a \textbf{radial bird closed set} or
a \textbf{radial bird particle} or simply a \textbf{radial bird}.

[Theorem lipG of arXiv:2607.00753, 'Threatening excursions in large population\\ quasi-stationary birth and death systems.\\ O'] Let $A$ and $G$ be open subsets of $\mathds R_{+}^{d}$ satisfying  Assumption {\bf (HS)}  and such that $A \Subset G$.   Then there exists a positive constant $K(A,G)$ such that for any $K\ge K(A,G)$,

(i) there exists a positive constant $ C(A,G)$ with
\begin{align*}
\sup_{{\underline n ;\,  d(\frac{\underline n}{K},A)\le  {1\over 2}  d(\partial A, \partial G)} }{{\mathds P}}^{({\scriptscriptstyle K})}_{\underline n} \big(T^{({\scriptscriptstyle K})}_{G}\le 1 \big) &\le e^{-C(A,G)\,K}\,; \\
\sup_{\underline n \in K*A }{{\mathds P}}^{({\scriptscriptstyle K})}_{\underline n}\big( {\underline N^{({\scriptscriptstyle K})}}(1)\in K*A^{c}\big)& \le e^{-C(A,G)\,K} \,;
\end{align*}
(ii) there exist positive constants  $C_{1}(A,G),   C_{2}(A,G),  \zeta(A,G)$ such that  for any $0<\zeta\le \zeta(A,G)$,
$$
\sup_{\underline z;\, d(\underline z,A)\le {1\over 2}d(\partial A, \partial G) }{{\mathds P}}^{({\scriptscriptstyle K})}_{[\underline z K]} \Big(\sup_{0\le t \le 1} \left\| \frac{{\underline N^{({\scriptscriptstyle K})}}(t)}{K}-\varphi_{t}(\underline z)\right\| >\zeta\Big) \le C_{1}(A,G)\,e^{-C_{2}(A,G) \,K\,\zeta}.
$$

