[Proposition 2 of arXiv:2606.06757, 'Path-Dependent Ergodic Optimal Control \\ and Backward Stochastic Differential Equations'] For all $K\in\K$, we have $\lambda_*(K^0) \le \lambda_*(K) \le \lambda^*(K) \le \lambda^*(K^0)$.
Moreover, 
\begin{center}
    \hspace{-5mm}
    {\rm (1)} $\lambda_*(K^0)=\lambda^*(K^0)$ iff {\rm (2)} $\lambda_*(K)=\lambda^*(K)$ for all $K\in\K$  iff {\rm (3)} $\lambda_*(K)=\lambda^*(K)$ for some $K\in\K_W$.
\end{center}
As a consequence, in either of these cases, we have $\lambda_*(K)=\lambda^*(K)=\lambda^*(K^0)$ for all $K\in\K$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

