body:
[Lemma lem:convergenceXtilde of arXiv:2411.13505, 'Capacity of loop-erased random walk'] Let 
\begin{equation}
    \begin{split}
        \widetilde{X}^+_n=&(\log n)^{1/3}\mathbb{P}_0^W(W[1,\infty)\cap\eta[1,n]=\varnothing\mid \eta),\\
        \widetilde{X}_n=&(\log n)^{1/3}\mathbb{P}_0^W(W[1,\infty)\cap\eta[0,n]=\varnothing\mid \eta),
    \end{split}
\end{equation}
Then $X_\infty=\lim_{n\rightarrow\infty} \widetilde{X}_n$ and $X_\infty^+=\lim_{n\rightarrow\infty}\widetilde{X}_n^+$ almost surely and in $L^p$ for every $p<3$.\footnote{It should be possible to prove $L^p$ convergence for all $p>0$, but we do not need it} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

