[Lemma lem: asymptotic uncorrelated of arXiv:2606.19583, 'Power-law hypothesis and (un)fairness of PageRank on undirected multi-type PAMs'] For any $k \in \{1,2\}$, any $\omega \in \{0,1,\ldots,m_k\}$ and any $d \in \{m_k,m_k+1,\ldots\}$,
as $n \to \infty$, the sequence of random variables 
\begin{equation}
\left(\mathbb{P}(d_{\phi_n}=d,d_{\phi_n}^{+,\mathrm{mino},(n)}=\omega,X_{\phi_n}=k \mid G_n)\right)_{n \in \mathbb{N}}     
\end{equation}
converges almost surely to
\begin{equation}
\mu_k \cdot \frac{2\Gamma(m_k+\frac{2}{\varphi_k})}{\varphi_k \Gamma(m_k)}\frac{\Gamma(d)}{\Gamma(d+\frac{2}{\varphi_k}+1)}\cdot \binom{m_k}{\omega}p^\omega_{\eta_k^{\boldsymbol{m}},k}(1-p_{\eta_k^{\boldsymbol{m}},k})^{m_k-\omega}.    
\end{equation}

