[Dfntn 11 of arXiv:2608.31054, 'Revisiting Picard's proof of the Picard--Weber--Weck selection theorem'] For $\mathcal{D} \subseteq D(\op A_0^\ast)$, we define the collection
    \begin{align}
        V_{\mathcal{D}} = \left\{ \psi \in \hilbert H_1 \,:\, \psi = \left(\op I - \op A_0 (\op A_0^\ast \op A_0 + \op I)^{-1} \op A_0^\ast \right) \phi\text{ for some } \phi \in \mathcal{D} \right\}.
