[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2605.27713, 'Lower path regularity in all dimensions'] If $\mu$ is a finite Borel measure on $\mathbb{R}^{d}$ such that $\mu\ll \mathcal{L}^d$, then 
		\begin{equation}
			\lim_{\alpha \to 0} \alpha\;U^{\alpha}\mu = d\:\omega_d\;\frac{d\mu}{d\mathcal{L}^d}\qquad \text{$\mu$-a.e.}
		\end{equation}
		If $L$ is a version of $\frac{d\mu}{d\mathcal{L}^d}$ which is bounded on $\mathbb{R}^d$ and 
		continuous at a point $x\in\mathbb{R}^d$, then $\lim_{\alpha \to 0} \alpha\;U^{\alpha}\mu(x)=d\:\omega_d\;L(x)$.

