[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2607.07022, 'Coordinate-wise Elephant Random Walk'] The total variation $\delta_n:=\sup_{x\in Q_k} ||K_n(x,\cdot)-K^{\star}(x,\cdot)||_{\TV}$, $n \ge 0$ satisfies  
    \begin{equation}
        \delta_n\leq \frac{1}{2}\max_{1\leq i \leq k} |\widehat{m}_n^{(i)}|.
    \end{equation}
     In particular, if $p_i<1$ for every $i$, then $\delta_n\to 0$ almost surely and in $L^1$, as $n \to \infty$.

