[Lemma 48 of arXiv:2605.02430, '\textbf{Scaling limit of the range of tree-valued branching random walks in random environ'] Let $\ccG\! \subset \! \ccF$ be a $\sigma$-field and let $(Z^{_{(n)}}_s)_{s\in \bbR_+}$, $n\ino \bbN^*$, be a sequence of $\bbR$-valued continuous processes such that $Z^{_{(n)}}_0\eqo 0$. Let $\ttb\ino (1, \infty)$ and $\gamma \ino (0, 1]$. Let us assume that for all $p\ino \bbN^*$, there exists a $\ccG$-measurable r.v.~$\mathtt C_p$ such that for all $n\ino \bbN^*$, 
\begin{equation}

\textrm{$\bP$-a.s.~} \quad \bE \big[ \big( \mathtt{Hol}_{\gamma , \, p} (Z^{_{(n)}}_{^{\,}} )\big)^\ttb  \big| \ccG\big] \leq \mathtt C_p < \infty \; .
\end{equation}  
Then conditionally given $\ccG$, the laws of the processes $(Z^{_{(n)}}_{^{\,}}\! )_{n\in \bbN^*}$ are a.s.~tight on $\bC^{0} (\bbR_+, \bbR)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 8 (Absolute inner shadowing) of arXiv:2609.02788, '\textbf{Quantized Einstein Metrics on \(S^7\) with \(SU(3)\)-Symmetry}'] For $s_0$ fixed sufficiently far inside the cone chart,
\begin{equation}
 \|U_{\PE}(s)-U_{\RF}(s)\|\le Cb^2e^{2s},
 \qquad s_0\le s\le s_b,
\end{equation}
uniformly for $|\mu|\le\mu_0$.

[Lemma l:capbounds of arXiv:2605.20587, 'Persistence and entropic repulsion of stationary Gaussian fields with spectral singularity'] For every $\gamma >  \gamma' > 0 $ there exist $c_d > 0$ and $T_0= T_0(d,\gamma, \gamma') > 0$ such that, for all $T \ge T_0$,
\[ \frac{1}{\mu[ B( (\log T)^{1+\gamma} / T ) ] + \|\mu \| e^{- (\log T)^{1+\gamma'}}}  \le \text{\textup{Cap}}(B(T))  \le  \frac{4}{  \mu[B(c_d / T) ] } .\]
Moreover, suppose that the doubling condition (equation e:doub of the paper) holds, and let $c_0 > 0$ be the constant in this condition. Then there exists a constant $c = c(d,c_0) > 0$ such that, for all $T \ge 1$,
\begin{equation}

 1/c \le \text{\textup{Cap}}(B(T)) \mu[B(1/ T) ]  \le c .
 \end{equation}

