[Definition def:gluing_of_fat of arXiv:2505.07145, 'Nonamenable Poisson zoo'] Let $A \subset \subset V(G)$ connected, $x \in \partial_{\mathrm{ext}} A$, and $\mathcal{X} = \sum_{i \in I} \delta_{(x,H)_i}$ a point measure. Then, for $i = 1,2$,
\begin{equation}

	\Phi_i(x, A, \mathcal{X}) := 
	\begin{cases}
		\Psi_i(x,A), & \text{if} \quad \forall \, y \in \{ x, \Psi_i(x,A) \}, \, \exists \, H \in \mathcal{H}_y: \, \mathcal{X}((y,H)) > 0; \\
		\emptyset, & \text{otherwise}.
	\end{cases}
\end{equation}
Again, this can be extended to any $B \subseteq \partial_{\mathrm{ext}} A$ as
\begin{equation}

	\Phi_i(B,A,\mathcal{X}) := \big\{ \Phi_i(x,A,\mathcal{X}) : {x \in B} \big\}.
\end{equation}

