body:
[Lemma right-adjoint-right-Bousfield of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] Let $S\subset T$ be a cleft and let $X\in\Spc_T$. Then the $S$-parametrized right adjoint $R$ of the inclusion $\ul\Spc_{S\triangleright T/X}\hookrightarrow\ul\Spc_{T/X}$ is $S$-cocontinuous. Moreover, if $X$ is equipped with a commutative monoid structure, then the lax symmetric monoidal structure on $R$ (with respect to the slice symmetric monoidal structures) is strong.
    \begin{proof}
        By [CLL_Clefts]*{Lemmas~3.16 and~3.17}, we have a right Bousfield localization ${\mathop{\textup{incl}}}\colon\ul\Spc_{S\triangleright T}|_S\rightleftarrows\ul\Spc_T|_S
	\nobreak
	\mspace{6mu plus 1mu}
	{:}
	\nonscript\mkern-\thinmuskip
	\mathpunct{}
	\mspace{2mu}
 r$. It follows formally that the Beck--Chevalley map
        \[
            \begin{tikzcd}
                (\ul\Spc_{T/X})|_S\arrow[r,"R"]\arrow[d,"\textup{fgt}"'] & (\ul\Spc_{S\triangleright T/X})|_S\arrow[d,"\textup{fgt}"]\arrow[dl,Rightarrow,shorten=10pt]\\
                (\ul\Spc_T)|_S\arrow[r,"r"'] & \ul\Spc_{S\triangleright T}|_S
            \end{tikzcd}
        \]
        is an equivalence. By [CLL_Clefts]*{Proposition 4.28}, the bottom map $r$ is $S$-cocontinuous; as the vertical maps are conservative and $S$-cocontinuous, we conclude that also $R$ is $S$-cocontinuous. Similarly, $r$ is strong symmetric monoidal with respect to the cartesian symmetric monoidal structures (being a right adjoint), so that $R$ is strong symmetric monoidal with respect to the the slice symmetric monoidal structures. 
    \end{proof}

