[Corollary rem:constantprefactor of arXiv:2505.12187, 'Speeding up quantum Markov processes through lifting'] Under the same assumptions as in (thm:flowpoincare of the paper), it holds that for any $T > 0$ and $x_0 \in \mathcal{F}^\perp$, 
    \begin{align} 
    \lVertP_t x_0\rVert_{\mathcal{H}} \le C e^{-\nu t} \lVertx_0\rVert_{\mathcal{H}}\,,
\end{align}
where $C = e^{\nu T}$, and $\nu$ satisfies (equation eq:ratel2 of the paper). Furthermore, for any $\gamma > 0$ and $T > 0$, we have 
\begin{equation*}
    C = e^{\nu T} = \mathcal{O}(1)\,,
\end{equation*}
if $K_0 K_3 = \Theta(1)$ holds, where  $K_0, K_3$ are the constants from (equation asspc0 of the paper)--(equation asspc2 of the paper).

