[Lemma lem:Gibbsprobability of arXiv:2411.18563, 'Lower tails for triangles inside the critical window'] In the setting of Theorem~(thm:barbour2019longterm of the paper), let us further suppose that $P$ is reversible with stationary distribution $\nu$, and let $\tilde{\Omega}_{\text{typ}} \subseteq \Omega_{\text{typ}}$. Then for any event $\mathcal{Q} \subseteq \Omega$, we have
\begin{equation}
\nu\left( \mathcal{Q}\wedge \tilde{\Omega}_{\text{typ}}\right) \leq \frac{\mathbb{P}_{\nu}\left(\{Y_k \in \mathcal{Q}\} \land \mathcal{A}_k\right)}{\min_{y \in \tilde{\Omega}_{\text{typ}}}\mathbb{P}_y(\mathcal{A}_k)}.
\end{equation}

