[Proposition prop:loc of arXiv:2607.20956, 'Sharp moduli of continuity for Gaussian fields and stochastic PDEs via correlation bounds'] Suppose (equation alphaH=3/2 of the paper), and set
    \begin{align*}
        \delta = h^{\rho\alpha} \quad \text{and} \quad
        \varepsilon= \delta^{\frac{2H+2}{3+2\alpha}}

        = h^{\rho}.
    \end{align*}
    Fix $0<t_1<t_2$. Then, there exists $K > 0$ such that for any $\rho \in (0\,,1)$, there exists $r_\rho \in (0\,,1)$ such that
    \begin{align*}
        \|\Delta^h_B u(t\,,x)\|_2^2 \le K \rho\, h^2 \log(1/h)
    \end{align*}
    uniformly for all $t \in [t_1\,,t_2]$, $x \in \mathbb{R}$ and $h \in (0\,,r_\rho]$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

