densities $f_{X},f_{Y}$. If $X\leq _{\mathrm{lr}}Y$, then $X\leq _{\mathrm{st
}}Y$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 434 of arXiv:2411.15485, '\bf\Large Stochastic Volterra Equations for Local Times of Spectrally Positive L\'evy Proc'] Assume that $G(t,y)=F(t)\cdot y$ for some locally bounded function $F$ on $\mathbb{R}_+$. 
 If  
 \begin{eqnarray}
   \int_0^\infty \frac{y^2}{n^2}\, \mu_n(dy) \to \sigma^2  \in (0,\infty)
 \quad \mbox{and}\quad 
 X^{(n)} \to X^* \in C(\mathbb{R}_+;\mathbb{R}_+) \mbox{ weakly in $D(\mathbb{R}_+;\mathbb{R}_+)$},
 \end{eqnarray} 
 as $n\to\infty$,   we have $Z^{(n)}  \overset{\rm f.d.d.}\longrightarrow Z^*$ with the limit process $Z^* $ given by
 \begin{eqnarray*}
 Z^*(t):= \int_0^t \int_0^{X^* (s)} F(t-s) B^* (ds,dz), \quad t\geq 0,
 \end{eqnarray*}  
 where $B^* (ds,dz)$ is Gaussian white noise with intensity $ \sigma^2\cdot ds\, dz$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

