[Lem trim_twist of arXiv:2608.30031, 'Ziggurats, taut foliations, and contact structures'] Let $\xi$ and $T$ be as above.
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item (Trim) There exists a positive contact structure $\xi'$ which is $C^\infty$-close to $\xi$ and such that $\partial \xi \prec \partial \xi'$ along $T$.
        \item (Twist) Suppose $\xi$ is $\Phi$-horizontal for some smooth nonsingular flow $\Phi$ on $M$. For any smooth $\Phi$-horizontal foliation $\mathcal{G}$ on $\partial M$ satisfying $\mathcal{G} \prec \partial \xi$, there is a $\Phi$-horizontal positive contact structure $\xi'$ with $\partial \xi' = \mathcal{G}$.
    \end{enumerate}
    In both cases, we can arrange that $\xi'$ coincides with $\xi$ away from an arbitrarily small neighborhood of $T$.

