[Theorem \cite{FNRW} of arXiv:2411.14818, 'Scaling limits of solitons in the Box-Ball system'] Let $X_{k}(n)$ be the position of the leftmost component of a tagged $k$-soliton at time $n$ and ${\mu}$ be a probability measure on $\{0,1\}^{{\mathbb{Z}}}$ satisfying the following. 
                \begin{itemize}
                    \item ${\mu}(\Omega) = 1$. 
                    \item ${\mu}$ is an invariant measure of the BBS, {namely $T{\mu}={\mu}$.}
                    \item ${\mu}$ is a shift-ergodic measure. 
                \end{itemize}
            Assume that for some $k \in {\mathbb{N}}$, $k$-solitons exist with positive probability under ${\mu}$. Then, there exists some $v^{\mathrm{eff}}_{k} =v^{\mathrm{eff}}_k({\mu}) > 0$ such that 
                \begin{align}
                    \lim_{n \to \infty} \frac{X_{k}(n)}{n} = v^{\mathrm{eff}}_{k} \quad {\mu}\text{-a.s.}
                \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

