[Lemma lem:radial-neighbour of arXiv:2608.30831, 'Sharp discrete Hardy constants in dimensions three and four\\ and strict upper bounds from'] Let $H:\mathbb N_0\to\mathbb R$, let $n\in\mathbb Z^N$, and put $s=|n|^2$.  Define
\begin{equation}
 \mu_r(n):=\#\{j\in\{1,\ldots,N\}: |n_j|=r\},\qquad r\in\mathbb N_0.
\end{equation}
Then
\begin{equation}
 \sum_{m\sim n}H(|m|^2)
 =2\mu_0(n)H(s+1)
 +\sum_{r\ge1}\mu_r(n)
   \bigl[H(s+1-2r)+H(s+1+2r)\bigr].
\end{equation}

[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2605.13518, 'The inertial It\^{o} drift and its applications to particle collision'] For every $p\geq 1$ and $T>0$, we have	
\begin{equation}
\sup_{\e\in\,(0,1)}\mathbb{E}\sup_{s \in\,[0,T]}\vert x_{\epsilon}(s)\vert^p \leq c_{p, T}.
\end{equation}
Moreover, the family $\{\mathcal{L}(x_{\e})\}_{\e \in\,(0,1)}$ is tight in $C([0,T];\mathbb{R}^d)$.

