body:
[Proposition 23 of arXiv:2608.02927, 'Thinning Operation via the Poisson-F\"ollmer Process'] (Equality cases of Thinning Lemma). Let $X$ be a random variable with density $f$ with respect to $\pi_{T}.$ Assume that $f : \N \rightarrow ( 0, \infty)$ satisfies $H( X | \pi_{T}) < \infty.$ Then, equality holds in the Thinning Lemma, i.e.,
    \begin{displaymath}
        H( T_{a}(X) | \pi_{aT}) = a H(X | \pi_{T} )
    \end{displaymath}
    for some $a \in (0,1)$ if and only if $f(k)=e^{\beta k + \gamma}$ for some $\beta ,\gamma \in \R$ (that is $X$ is Poisson distributed).

