\end{equation}
for any $\kappa>0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma Holder prop for int ell of arXiv:2412.08932, 'Gaussian heat kernel asymptotics for conditioned random walks'] There exists a constant $c>0 $ such that, for any $x, x' \in \bb R$ with $|x-x'|\leqslant 1$, 
and any measurable set $D\subseteq \bb R$,
 \begin{align*} 
\left| \int_D \ell_h(x', y) dy  -  \int_D \ell_h(x, y) dy \right|  \leqslant c L(x) |x-x'|. 
\end{align*}

