[Thm 1 (\cites{Rei77, ESI92}) of arXiv:2608.26723, 'Extrinsic upper bounds for the harmonic mean of eigenvalues in curved manifolds'] Let $M$ be an $m(\ge 2)$-dimensional closed orientable submanifolds in a space form $\mathbb{R}^{n}(c)$. Then the first nonzero eigenvalue $\lambda_1$  of the Laplacian on $M$ satisfies
	\begin{equation}
		\lambda_1\leq\frac{m}{\vol(M)}\int_M(c+|\mathbf{H}|^2),
	\end{equation}
	where $\mathbf{H}$ is the mean curvature vector of $M$ in $\mathbb{R}^{n}(c)$.

	Equality holds if and only if $M$ is either minimally immersed in $\mathbb{S}^n$ by a subspace of the first eigenspace, or minimally immersed in a geodesic sphere of $\mathbb{R}^{n}(c)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:two_edge_1_gamma_minus_1_le_delta_le_1_gamma of arXiv:2509.23496, 'Crossing probabilities in geometric inhomogeneous random graphs'] Suppose $\frac 1 \gamma-1<\delta<\frac 1 \gamma$. The two-edge crossing probabilities are given~by 
    \begin{align*}
        \pi_{(u),R}^{(2)} 
        &\asymp \pi_{(u),R}+ u^{-\gamma} R^{d(1+\frac 1{\gamma \delta}-\frac 1 \gamma-\frac 1 {\delta})}\wedge 1\\
        &\asymp \begin{cases}
                    u^{-\gamma} R^{d(1+\frac 1{\gamma \delta}-\frac 1 \gamma-\frac 1 {\delta})} & \text{ on } \{u  \geq R^{-d\frac {\delta+1-1/\gamma}{\gamma \delta}} \},\\
                    u^{-\gamma \delta} R^{d(1-\delta)} & \text{ on } \{R^{d(\frac 1 {\gamma \delta}-\frac 1 \gamma)}  \leq u  \leq R^{-d(\frac {\delta+1-1/\gamma}{\gamma \delta})} \},\\
                    1 & \text{ on } \{u \leq R^{d(\frac 1 {\gamma \delta}-\frac 1 \gamma)} \}.
                \end{cases}
    \end{align*}
    \begin{align*}
       \pi_{r,R}^{(2)} 
        &\asymp \pi_{r,R}+ r^{\frac d \delta} R^{d(1+\frac 1{\gamma \delta}-\frac 1 \gamma-\frac 1 {\delta})}
        \asymp \begin{cases}
                    r^{\frac d \delta} R^{d(1+\frac 1{\gamma \delta}-\frac 1 \gamma-\frac 1 {\delta})} & \text{ on } 
                    \{  r \leq R^{1+\delta-\frac 1 \gamma}\},\\
                    r^d R^{d(1-\delta)} & \text{ on } \{  R^{1+\delta-\frac 1 \gamma} \leq r \leq R/2\}.
                \end{cases}
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

