[Lemma lem:2 of arXiv:2412.09290, 'Asymptotics of Harish-Chandra transform and infinitesimal freeness'] For a smooth function $f$ of $N$ variables we have
  \begin{equation}
    \mathcal{D}_k (f) = \sum_{m = 0}^k \sum_{\underset{l_i \neq l_j \text{ for
    } i \neq j}{l_0, \ldots, l_m = 1}}^N \binom{k}{m} \frac{\partial_{l_0}^{k
    - m} f}{(x_{l_0} - x_{l_1}) \ldots (x_{l_0} - x_{l_m})} .

  \end{equation}

