body:
[Lemma 32 (Separated-support smoothing) of arXiv:2607.10813, '2607.10813'] Let $\phi\in C_c^\infty(\R^3)$ and $\psi\in C_b^\infty(\R^3)$ satisfy
$d_0:=\dist(\supp\phi,\supp\psi)>0$.  If
$f,g\in C([0,T];\mathfrak T_{J_{\mathrm{ps}}})$, then the three localized
inhomogeneous Bony series
\[
  \phi((\psi f)\prec g),\qquad \phi((\psi f)\succ g),\qquad \phi((\psi f)\circ g)
\]
converge in $C([0,T];H^M\cap\mathcal C^M)$ for every $M>0$, and
\begin{equation}
 \sup_{t\le T}\sum_{\star\in\{\prec,\succ,\circ\}}
 \|\phi((\psi f)\star g)(t)\|_{H^M\cap\mathcal C^M}
 \le C_{M,J_{\mathrm{ps}},d_0,\phi,\psi}
 \|f\|_{C_T\mathfrak T_{J_{\mathrm{ps}}}}
 \|g\|_{C_T\mathfrak T_{J_{\mathrm{ps}}}}.
\end{equation}
The same estimate is uniform after admissible spectral truncations are inserted
on either factor.  Convergence in $C_T\mathfrak T_{J_{\mathrm{ps}}}$ passes to
the corresponding localized Bony series in every displayed topology.

