{"artifact_digest":"sha256:13e26dcffa4deff36e43be222667a80462a117619a1cb6cdfb98c09dc5c0a166","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/13/13e26dcffa4deff36e43be222667a80462a117619a1cb6cdfb98c09dc5c0a166.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:05f32c6a14012228d1a6f5c4a03a590dfa205bbc605ef032ca359d8bc9ecc16d","bundle_entry_key":"2606-14876-lemma-30-phi-max-location","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s3_050","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s3_050.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2606-14876-lemma-30-phi-max-location","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: Write $\varphi_a(x):=\frac{1-\upe^{-x}}{x^{a}}$. Then for $x>0$,
\begin{equation*}
    \varphi_a^{\prime}(x) = x^{-a-1} \upe^{-x} \left( x- a\left(\upe^x-1\right)\right).
\end{equation*}
\begin{itemize}
    \item When $a=1$, for all $x>0$, note that $\upe^x-1\geq x$, we have
    \begin{equation*}
        \varphi_1^{\prime}(x) = x^{-a-1} \upe^{-x} \left( x- \left(\upe^x-1\right)\right)  \leq 0.
