[Corollary 35 of arXiv:2609.03403, 'Hyperpositive functions, sector bounded functions and a trace formula'] Let $F\in\mathcal{HP}_{T,t}$ with representation \eqref{repre-321-11}. Then, 
            \begin{equation}

F^{-1}(z)=T^{-1}+(T^{-1}+tT)S(z)T^{-1/2}
              \end{equation}
where $S$ is defined by \eqref{Snew}. Furthermore, $S$ is bounded if and only $t<0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2511.06196, 'Central limit theorem for high temperature spin models via martingale embedding'] Let \(A \subset \{1,\ldots,n\}\) and choose arbitrary \(\epsilon > 0\).
Then, for some \(C_{t,\epsilon}, c_\epsilon > 0\), independent of \(n\) and \(A\), we have
\begin{equation*}
\sup_{\sigma \in \{-1,1\}^{A}}
\E\Big|\sum_{j=1}^nm_{ijk}^{[A]}\Big|^{2+\epsilon}
\le \frac{C_{t,\epsilon}}{n^{1+\epsilon/2}}
\end{equation*}
for all $i\ne k$ and \(0 \le t < c_\epsilon\). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

