[Theorem 23 (Uniform-in-time propagation of chaos in Langevin KSD) of arXiv:2608.28827, 'Quantitative Target Convergence and Uniform-in-Time\\ Propagation of Chaos for Langevin-Re'] Under Assumptions~\ref{ass:core-target},
\ref{ass:ksd-kernel}, and \ref{ass:concentration}, let $L_\mathrm{cpl}>0$ be the coupling exponent
obtained from Proposition~\ref{prop:refined-coupling} under these assumptions.
Then there is $C<\infty$ such that
\begin{equation}
\sup_{t\ge0}\E\KSD_\pi(\mu_t^N,\mu_t)
\le C\left\{
N^{-\frac{\varepsilon\alpha}{L_\mathrm{cpl}+2\varepsilon\alpha}}
+N^{-1/2}\right\},

\end{equation}

[Definition NS-def sol of arXiv:2605.28194, 'Delayed Blow-up in 3D Fluids via Pseudo-Transport Noise'] Given a filtered probability space $(\Omega,\mathcal{F},(\mathcal{F}_t),\mathbb{P})$ and a sequence of independent $(\mathcal{F}_t)$-Brownian motion $\{W^k\}$, we say an $(\mathcal{F}_t)$-progressively measurable process $u$ is a strong solution to (equation NS-u of the paper) if the following holds:
		\begin{itemize}
			\item[(1).] $u\in C([0,T]; H^{2b+a})\cap L^2(0,T; H^{2b+a+1}),\:\mathbb{P}$-a.s.
			\item[(2).] For every divergence-free vector field $\varphi\in C^\infty (\mathbb{T}^3;\mathbb{R}^3)$, $\mathbb{P}$-a.s. the following identity holds:
			\begin{equation*}
				\begin{split}
					\<u(t),\varphi\> &=\<u_0,\varphi\>-\int_{0}^t\<u\cdot\nabla u, \varphi\>\,{\,\rm d} s + \<u,\Delta \varphi\>\,{\,\rm d} t\\
					&\quad- \sum_k\int_{0}^t\big\<u, (-\Delta)^{2b+a}\mathcal{L}_k (-\Delta)^{-2b-a}\varphi\big\> \circ {\,\rm d} W_s^k,\quad \text{ for all } t\in [0,T].
				\end{split}
			\end{equation*}
		\end{itemize}

