[Theorem 31 of arXiv:2609.03403, 'Hyperpositive functions, sector bounded functions and a trace formula'] Let      $(A_\zeta,\mathcal B_-,\mathcal B_+)\in\mathbb C^{a_\zeta\times a_\zeta}\times\times\mathbb C^{a_\zeta\times m}\times\mathbb C^{a_\zeta\times m}$ with
      $\sigma(A_\zeta)\subset\mathbb C_r$. There exists a
      $\mathbb C^{m\times m}$-valued function $\sigma$ analytic and contractive in $\mathbb C_r$
      and such that
\begin{equation}

  \sum_{z_0\in\mathbb C_r} {\rm Res}_{{z}=z_0}\,(zI_{a_\zeta}-A_\zeta)^{-1}\mathcal  B_+\sigma(z)=-\mathcal  B_-.
\end{equation}
            if and only if the unique solution of the Lyapunov equation
            \begin{equation}

    GA_\zeta^*+A_\zeta G=\mathcal B_+\mathcal B_+^*-\mathcal B_-\mathcal B_-^*
      \end{equation}
  is strictly positive. When this condition is in force, the set of solutions is given by the formula
  \begin{equation}
\sigma(z)=(\Theta_{11}(z)\widetilde{\sigma}(z)+\Theta_{12}(z))(\Theta_{21}(z)\widetilde{\sigma}(z)+\Theta_{22}(z))^{-1}
  \end{equation}
  where
  \begin{equation}

    \Theta(z)=I_{2m}+\begin{pmatrix}-\mathcal B_+^*\\ \mathcal B_-^*\end{pmatrix}
    (zI_{a_\zeta}+A_\zeta^*)^{-1}G^{-1}\begin{pmatrix}\mathcal B_+&\mathcal B_-\end{pmatrix},
  \end{equation}
  and where $\widetilde{\sigma}$ runs through the set of $\mathbb C^{m\times m}$-valued functions analytic and strictly contractive in $\mathbb C_r$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

