[Theorem 2 of arXiv:2506.18063, 'Reduced critical branching processes in non-favorable random environment \thanks{ This wor'] Assume that Conditions $B1$ and $B2$ are valid. If $
k\sim \theta m=\theta m(n)\rightarrow \infty $ as $n\rightarrow \infty $ in
such a way that $m=o(n)$, then, for any $y\geq 0$ and $t>0$
\begin{equation}
\lim_{n\gg k\rightarrow \infty }\mathbf{P}\left( \log Z_{r,n}\leq ya_{m}|
\mathcal{R}\left( ta_{k},n\right) \right) =A(\theta ^{1/\alpha }t,\theta
^{1/\alpha }\left( t\wedge y\right) ),  
