[Proposition 5 ({\cite{LR10},\cite[Theorem 3.1) of arXiv:2510.27589, 'Geodesic switches and exceptional times in dynamical Brownian last passage percolation'] {DV21+}}]

  Fix $k\in \NN$. Then for some constants $C_1,C_2,c_1,c_2$ depending on $k$, for all $x>0$ and for all $0 < \alpha < 5n^{2/3}$, we have
  \begin{align}

    \PP(P_{k,n}(x)\geq 2\sqrt{nx}+ \alpha\sqrt{x}n^{-1/6}) &\leq C_1e^{-c_1\alpha^{3/2}},\nonumber\\
    \PP(P_{k,n}(x)\leq 2\sqrt{nx}- \alpha\sqrt{x}n^{-1/6}) &\leq C_2e^{-c_2\alpha^{3}}.
  \end{align}
  Further, for some $k$-dependent constants $C_3,c_3$, all $\alpha \geq 5n^{2/3}$ and all $n$, we have
  \begin{equation}

    \PP(|P_{k,n}(x)-2\sqrt{nx}|\geq \alpha \sqrt{x} n^{-1/6})\leq C_3e^{-c_3\alpha^2 n^{-1/3}}.
  \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Prop thin-chaos of arXiv:2602.06011, 'Excursion decomposition of the XOR-Ising model'] Let $\alpha\in(0,1)$. For any $a<a_c(\alpha)$, let $\mathds A_{-a,a}$ be a subcritical two-valued set in a valid domain $D$. For any continuous, bounded  function $f:\mathbb C\to\mathbb R$, 
    \begin{align}
    \lim_{n\to \infty} (\field{e^{i\alpha \phi}}, f\1_{[\mathds A_{-a, a}]_n}) =0, 
    \end{align}
    where the limit is in probability.

