[Lemma lem:inf_rate of arXiv:2604.14851, 'Pool model: a mass preserving multi particle aggregation process'] Consider stopping time 
	$$
	\Delta\tau=\inf\{t>0, \tilde A^R_t\cap B(R)\not=\emptyset \}
	$$
	be the first time that a particle enters the ball of radius $R$. Then there is some constant $C<\infty$ such that for all $R\ge \pi^{-1/2}$ and $t\ge 0$, we have 
	\begin{equation}\begin{aligned}

	r(R,t):=\lim_{\Delta t\to0}\frac{P(\Delta\tau\in (t,t+\Delta t]|\Delta\tau>t)}{\Delta t}\le r(R,0)\le CR. 
	\end{aligned}\end{equation}

[Lemma lemma_overline_alpha_sigma_long_enough of arXiv:2605.26804, '\Large Large Deviation Principle for the Empirical Measures of Simple Random Walks on $\ov'] Fix $\sigma \in \{-,0,+\}$ and $w \in \Omega_n^{(0)}(\mu,2^{-R}\varepsilon)$. If $\#J^{\sigma} \neq 0$, then
\begin{equation}
\sum_{h=1}^{\#J^{\sigma}}|u^{h,\sigma}|+\#J^{\sigma}-1 < \overline{\alpha}_{\sigma,n}.
\end{equation}

