body:
[Lemma lem.dpp of arXiv:2605.14149, 'The mean-field limit of online stochastic vector balancing'] Fix integers $0\leq k_0 < k_1 \leq n$ and $\bm{x} \in {\mathbb R}^n$. Let $(\Omega, \mathcal{F}, \mathbb{P})$ be a probability space, and $\mathbb{G} = (\mathcal{G}(k))_{k = k_0,\dots,k_1}$ be a filtration of $\mathcal{F}$. Furthermore, let $(\bm{Z}(k))_{k = k_0+1,\dots,k_1}$ be a sequence of $\mathbb{G}$-adapted, ${\mathbb R}^n$-valued random vectors such that $\bm{Z}(k) \sim \nu_{1/n}^{\otimes n}$ is independent of $\mathcal{G}(k-1)$ for all $k = k_0+1,\dots,k_1$.
    Then, we have
    \begin{align*}
        \mathcal{V}^n(k_0,\bm{x}) =  \inf_{\varepsilon(k_0+1),\dots,\varepsilon(k_1)} {\mathbb E}\bigg[ \mathcal{V}^n\Big(k_1, \bm{x} + \sum_{k = k_0+1}^{k_1} \varepsilon(k) \bm{Z}(k)\Big) \bigg],
    \end{align*}
    where the infimum is taken over all $\mathbb{G}$-adapted $\{\pm 1\}$-valued processes $(\varepsilon(k))_{k = k_0+1,\dots,k_1}$. In particular, if $k_1 = n$, we have
    \begin{align*}
    \mathcal{V}^n(k_0,\bm{x}) = \inf_{\varepsilon(k_0+1),\dots,\varepsilon(n)} {\mathbb E}\,\Big| \bm{x} + \sum_{k = k_0+1}^n \varepsilon(k) \bm{Z}(k) \Big|_{\infty},
    \end{align*}
    and thus, $V^n = \mathcal{V}^n(0,\bm{0})$, where $V^n$ was defined in (equation def.vn.intro of the paper).

