[Corollary 7 of arXiv:2506.13913, '2506.13913'] {}{BrownianHeatDensity}
Let \(\{W_t\}_{t \geq 0}\) be a \(d\)-dimensional Brownian motion starting at $x$, then its transition density $p_x(t, y)$ satisfies the equation 
\begin{equation}
 \frac{\partial p}{\partial t} = \frac{1}{2}\,\Delta p, \quad x \in \mathbb{R}^d, \, t > 0,   
\end{equation}
with initial condition $p(0,x, y)=\delta(y-x).$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

