[Problem 30 of arXiv:2609.03403, 'Hyperpositive functions, sector bounded functions and a trace formula'] Given  matrices
  \begin{equation}

(A_\zeta,B_-,B_+)\in\mathbb C^{a_\zeta\times a_\zeta}\times\mathbb C^{a_\zeta\times m}\times\mathbb C^{a_\zeta\times m},
\end{equation}
where the spectrum  of $A_\zeta$ is in $\mathbb C_r$, find all $\mathbb C^{m\times m}$-valued functions $F\in\mathcal {HP}_{T,t}$, such that
\begin{equation}

F(z)+F(z)^*+tT-F(z)TF(z)^* > 0, \quad z\in\mathbb C_r,
  \end{equation}
  and
\begin{equation}

  \sum_{z_0\in\mathbb C_r} {\rm Res}_{{z}=z_0}\,({z}I_{a_\zeta}-A_\zeta)^{-1}B_+F(z)=-B_-.
\end{equation} (Stated as a problem by the paper; open unless the paper says otherwise.)

