[Proposition 13 of arXiv:2603.25400, 'One-arm probabilities for the two-dimensional metric-graph and discrete Gaussian free fiel'] For any $h\le 0$, $x>0$, and $r\in(0,1/2]$, we have
    \begin{equation}
        g_{N,r}^h(x)\asymp\frac{x|h|}{\sqrt{\log N}}\nabla\frac{x|\log r|^{\frac12}}{\sqrt{\log N}}.
    \end{equation}
    Moreover, there exist $c,c',c''>0$ such that if $h>0, x\le c''\sqrt{\log N}\ |\log r|^{-\frac12}$, setting $K=K(h,r):=h|\log r|^{-\frac12}$, we have
    \begin{equation}
        xe^{-cK^2}\sqrt{\frac{|\log r|}{\log N}}\lesssim g_{N,r}^h(x)\lesssim xe^{-c'K^2}\sqrt{\frac{|\log r|}{\log N}}.
    \end{equation}

[Theorem 7 of arXiv:2605.14254, '2605.14254'] The $\mathbb{F}^{\xi^{\lambda,z}}$-predictable compensator associated with $\sigma_z^{\lambda}$ is
		\begin{equation}
			A_t^{\lambda,z}=\lambda\,L^{\lambda,z}(t\wedge \sigma_z^{\lambda},z).
		\end{equation}

