[Proposition 21 of arXiv:2608.19065, 'Boundedly exchangeable graphs'] For any $B\in\widehat{\Bcal}(S)$ with $\pbb(\nu(B)=0)<1$, there exists a graphon $W_B : [0,1]^2 \to [0,1]$ such that every exchangeable matrix $A^B$ associated with $\xi$ on $B$ admits a representation
    \begin{equation}
        A^B_{ij} \overset{a.s.}{=} \mathbf{1}\{U_{ij}\le W_B(U_i,U_j)\}, \qquad i,j \in \nbb.
