[Lemma w infity of arXiv:2606.29352, 'Exponential Mixing for 2D Stochastic Damped Euler Equation Driven by Bounded Noise'] Let $\gamma>0$. 
  If $w_0 \in W^{1,\infty}$, then 
 \begin{equation*}
     \sup_{t\geq0}\| w(t)\Vert_{\infty} < \infty,\; \mathbb{P}-a.s. \end{equation*}
     Moreover, there exist $R(\gamma)$ such that 
     \begin{equation}
          \|w(t)\Vert_{L^\infty} \leq  \|w_0\Vert_\infty\cdot e^{-\frac{\gamma t}{2}}+R,\;  \mathbb{P}-a.s. .     
        \end{equation}

