[Theorem theo:1Gllaw of arXiv:2605.21265, 'The non-Hermitian minor process'] Let $X$ satisfy Assumption~(ass:chi of the paper)(i). Fix a (large) $L>0$ and a (small) $c_0>0$. There exists an $N$-independent constant $\tau>0$ such that
\begin{align}
\left\vert\left\langle \big(G^{(k),z}_x(w)-M^{(k),z}_x(w)\big)B\right\rangle\right\vert &\prec\frac{\|B\|}{N\eta},\\
\left\vert\left\langle \bm{x}, \big(G^{(k),z}_x(w)-M^{(k),z}_x(w)\big)\bm{y}\right\rangle\right\vert &\prec\|\bm{x}\|\|\bm{y}\|\left(\sqrt{\frac{\rho_x^{z}(w)}{N\eta}}+\frac{1}{N\eta}\right),
\end{align}
uniformly in deterministic matrix $B\in\mathbf{C}^{(2k)\times (2k)}$, deterministic vectors $\bm{x},\bm{y}\in\mathbf{C}^{2k}$, $x:=k/N\in [c_0,1]$, $|\Re w|\le \tau$, $\eta:=|\Im w|\in (N^{-L}, N^L)$ and $|z|\le L$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 33 of arXiv:2607.21374, 'Local structure at the maximum and sharp persistence asymptotics of rough fractional Brown'] For every \(\lambda>0\), there is \(C_{H,\lambda}<\infty\) such that, for
every finite \(F\subset\mathbb D\), every \(e\in F\cup\{0\}\), and either
\(I=[0,1]\) or \(I=[-1,0]\),
\begin{equation}
  \EE_{\widehat Q_{F,e}}
  \exp\left(\lambda\sup_{t\in I}G_t\right)
  \leq C_{H,\lambda},

\end{equation}
uniformly in \(F\), \(e\), and the side.

[Lemma lemma-one-pt-estimate-interface-discrete of arXiv:2606.13147, 'Scaling limits of the single-curve interface and outermost loops in the planar random fiel'] Let $0 < \rho \ll 1$. There exist $\delta_0 > 0$ and an absolute constant $C>0$ such that for any $0 < \delta < \delta_0$, any $x \in \delta \mathbb{Z}^2$ and any $r > 0$,
    \begin{equation*}
        \mu_{\delta, \Lambda_{\delta}}^{\pm}[{\operatorname{dist}}(x,\gamma_{\delta}) \leq r] \leq C \bigg( \frac{r}{{\operatorname{dist}}(x,\partial \Lambda_{\delta})}\bigg)^{\frac{5}{8}-\rho}
    \end{equation*}
    where $\Lambda_{\delta} \subset \delta\mathbb{Z}^2$ is any square centered at $x$ and where under $\mu_{\delta, \Lambda_{\delta}}^{\pm}$, the Ising model in $\Lambda_{\delta}$ has $-1$ boundary conditions on the bottom side of $\Lambda_{\delta}$ and $+1$ boundary conditions everywhere else.

[Lemma 222 (Estimates for the error integrals generated by the weight) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] Assume that $1 \le N \le \Ntop, \, v \in \velocityarray = \{v^1,v^2,v^3\}$. Let $\tander^N \in \mathfrak{P}^{(N)}$, where $\mathfrak{P}^{(N)}$
is the set of order $N$ $\nullhyparg{u}$-tangential commutator operators from
