[Lemma 20 of arXiv:2608.15616, '\textbf{Compact Support Property of Super-Brownian Motion with Irregular Drift}'] Let $n\geq 2$ and $t \geq 0$. 
		Then we have the estimate 
		\begin{equation*}
        \begin{split}
			K_t^n &= 	\int_0^t\frac{1}{\sqrt{t-t_{n-1}}}\int_0^{t_{n-1}} \frac{1}{\sqrt{t_{n-1}-t_{n-2}}} \cdots \int_0^{t_1} \sqrt{t_1-t_0}dt_0 \cdots dt_{n-1} \\
            &=  \frac{2}{3}2^{n-1}\Big(\prod_{k=2}^{n}w_{k+2}\Big)t^{(n+2)/2},
        \end{split}
		\end{equation*}
		where $w_i = \int_0^{\pi/2} \sin^i(r)dr$ for $i \geq 2$.

