[Proposition jtpdf of arXiv:2605.27949, 'Yaglom limits of continuous-state branching processes in Brownian random environment \than'] For any $t>0,$ the joint probability density function of $A_t^{(\eta)}$ and $\left(\eta t+B^{(e)}_t\right)$ is given by
\begin{eqnarray*}
\!\!\!&\!\!\!&\mathbb P\left(A_t^{(\eta)} \in \mathrm{d} y, \eta t+B^{(e)}_t \in \mathrm{d} x\right) =\mathrm{e}^{\eta x-\frac{1}{2} \eta^2t} \frac{1}{y} \exp \left(-\frac{1+\mathrm{e}^{2 x}}{2 y}\right) \theta\left(\frac{\mathrm{e}^x}{y}, t\right) \mathrm{d} y \mathrm{d} x,
\end{eqnarray*}
where $$\theta(r, t)=\frac{r}{\sqrt{2 \pi^3 t}} \int_0^{\infty} \mathrm{e}^{\frac{\pi^2-u^2}{2 t}} \mathrm{e}^{-r \cosh u}\sinh (u) \sin \left(\frac{\pi u}{t}\right) \mathrm{d} u,\quad r>0,\,t>0.$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma random_walk_expected_hitting_size_main_text of arXiv:2608.00399, 'The Heavy-tailed Frog Model'] Consider a random walk on $\mathbb Z^d$ driven by $Q \in \mathcal{H}_{\alpha, K}$ starting from $x \in \mathbb Z^d$.
    Then, there exists a constant $c' = c'(K, \alpha, d)$ such that for any integer $r > 0$ and any $D \subseteq B_x(4r)$ with $|D| \ge r^d/4$, we have
    \begin{align}
        \sum_{y \in D} \mathbf P_y \left( \tau_x \le \ell(r) \right) \ge c' f(r),
    \end{align}
    where $ \ell(r) $ is defined in (equation def: s(r) of the paper) and $f(r)$ is defined as in Lemma~(lemma: range_estimates_main_text of the paper).

