[Theorem 6 (=Theorem \ref{thm:ax-nondeg}) of arXiv:2608.30174, 'Exact counting of spherical metrics with one conical singularity on rectangular tori'] Let $n\in\mathbb{N}_{\geq 1}$, $\rho\in (8\pi(n-1), 8\pi n)$ and $u(z)$ be a solution of \eqref{eq:mfe}, which is axisymmetric. Then 
\begin{equation}
\begin{cases}
\Delta \phi+e^u\phi=0\quad\text{on }E_{\ii b}\\
\phi(z)=\phi(-z)=\phi(\bar z)
\end{cases}
\end{equation}
has only trivial solutions. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma LEM:TGRAM of arXiv:2512.23957, 'Concentration and fluctuations of sine-Gordon measure around topological multi-soliton man'] Let $t_1,\dots, t_k$ be obtained by applying the Gram–Schmidt orthonormalization in $L^2$ to $\partial_{\xi_1}m^\varepsilon_{\xi_1,\dots,\xi_k}, \dots, \partial_{\xi_k} m^\varepsilon_{\xi_1,\dots, \xi_k}$, as described in (equation GRAM of the paper). Then, for each $j$, we have 
\begin{align*} 
|t_j(x)| \lesssim e^{-c|x-\xi_j|}
\end{align*}

\noindent
provided that $\min_{i \neq j}|\xi_i-\xi_j| \ge d$ for $d$ sufficiently large.

