[Lem lemma:frostman of arXiv:2509.06730, 'Hyperbolic branching Brownian motion: \\ the empirical limit measure'] Let $A$ be a compact subset of Euclidean space. Assume that there exists a probability measure $\nu$ on $A$ such that
    \begin{equation*}
        \iint_{A\times A} \vert x-y\vert^{-\eta} \nu(dx)\nu(dy) < \infty,
    \end{equation*}
    where $\eta >0$. Then the Hausdorff dimension of $A$ is at least $\eta$.

