body:
[Lemma lemma_prop_hitting of arXiv:2412.05706, 'Quasi-multiplicativity and regularity for metric graph Gaussian free fields'] For any $N\ge 1$, $D\subset \widetilde{B}(N)$, $x\in \partial B(2N)$ and $D'\subset [\widetilde{B}(3N)]^c$,
	\begin{equation}
		\widetilde{\mathbb{P}}_x(\tau_D<\tau_{D'})\asymp N^{2-d}\mathrm{cap}(D).
	\end{equation}
	Especially, when $D=\widetilde{B}(n)$ with $n\le N$, one has 
	\begin{equation}
		\widetilde{\mathbb{P}}_x(\tau_{\widetilde{B}(n)}<\tau_{D'})\asymp \big(\frac{n}{N}\big)^{d-2}.
	\end{equation}

