body:
[Theorem thm_mst_max of arXiv:2608.08529, 'Maximum Spanning Trees of Random Geometric Graphs With Independent Edge Weights'] Let~\(\epsilon_1,\epsilon_2\) be as in~((f_eq of the paper)) and suppose~\(nr_n^2p_n \geq M\log{n}\) for
some constant~\(M  >0.\) Also let~\(E_{con}\) denote the event that~\(G\) is connected.\\
\((a)\)  There  are constants~\(\gamma_0,\gamma_1 > 0\) such that if~\(M > \gamma_0,\) then
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{P}\left(E_{con} \bigcap \left\{\tau_n \geq \gamma_1 n H\left(\gamma_1nr_n^2p_n\right)\right\} \right) \geq 1-e^{-\gamma_1 nr_n^2p_n}
\end{equation}
and~\(\mathbb{E}\tau_n \geq \gamma_1 n H\left(\gamma_1nr_n^2p_n\right).\)\\
\((b)\) Suppose there are constants~\(C, x_0 > 0\) and~\(s > 2\) strictly, such that
\begin{equation}
F_c(ax) \leq \frac{C}{a^{s}}F_c(x)
\end{equation}
all~\(a > 1\) and~\(x > x_0.\) There are constants~\(\gamma_2,\gamma_3 > 0\) such that if~\(M > \gamma_2\) then
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{P}\left(E_{con} \bigcap \left\{\tau_n \leq \gamma_2 n H\left(nr_n^2p_n\right)\right\} \right) \geq 1-\frac{1}{(n^2r_n^2p_n)^{\gamma_3}}
\end{equation}
and~\(\mathbb{E}\tau_n \leq \gamma_2nH(nr_n^2p_n).\) (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem Thm-Blowup of arXiv:2609.01964, 'The critical exponent for the two-dimensional semilinear wave equation with strong damping'] Let $2<p\leqslant p_{\mathrm{crit}}=\frac{10}{3}$. Assume that $u_0,u_1\in\mathcal C_0^\infty$ satisfy
	\begin{align}
		M_1:=\int_{\mathbb{R}^2}u_1(x)\,\mathrm{d} x>0.
	\end{align}
	Then the maximal mild Sobolev solution to (equation Main-Problem of the paper) satisfies $T_{\max}<\infty$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem thm:eventuallyuniversaltiles of arXiv:2605.02226, 'Finitely Dependent Processes on Subshifts'] The following are equivalent:
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item There is $k_0 \in \mathbb{N}$ such that $\mathcal{R}$ tiles $R_{\ell}$ for every $\ell=(\ell_1,\dots,\ell_d)$ such that $\ell_1,\dots,\ell_d\ge k_0$.
        \item For every partition $\mathcal{R}=A_1\sqcup\dots\sqcup A_d$, (where some of the $ A_i$'s are possibly empty) there is $1\le j\le d$ such that
        $$\gcd\left(n_j(R):R \in A_j\right)=1.$$
    \end{enumerate}

