[Proposition of arXiv:2511.01851, 'Percolation on graphs of polynomial growth is local:\\analyticity, supercritical sharpness'] The following statements are equivalent:
    \begin{itemize}
        \item every graph in $\mathfrak{A}$ satisfies $\theta(p_c)=0$,
        \item for every sequence $(\mathscr{G})_{n\leqslant \infty}$ of elements of $\mathfrak{A}$ satisfying $\mathscr{G}_n\xrightarrow[n\to\infty]{}\mathscr{G}_\infty$, we have uniform convergence of $\tilde\theta_{\mathscr{G}_n}$ to $\tilde\theta_{\mathscr{G}_\infty}$.
    \end{itemize}

