body:
[Definition Definition_block_process of arXiv:2411.10829, 'Airy$_\beta$ line ensemble and its Laplace transform'] Take $m\in \mathbb N$, $\vec \mathbf k=(\mathbf k_1,\ldots, \mathbf k_m)\in \mathbb R_+^m$, and denote $\mathbf Q_\ell=\sum_{\ell'=1}^\ell \mathbf k_{\ell'}$ for each $\ell \in \llbracket 0, m\rrbracket$.
A \emph{block process with times $\vec \mathbf k$}
is a family $\vec \mathbf p=\{\mathbf p_j\}_{j=1}^{m+\mathbf u}$, where  $\mathbf u\in \mathbb Z_{\ge 0}$, and each $\mathbf p_j:[0, \mathbf Q_m]\to \mathbb R_{\ge 0}$ is a function satisfying the following:
\begin{itemize}
    \item for each $\ell \in \llbracket 1, m\rrbracket$, $\mathbf p_\ell\in \mathfrak B([0,\mathbf Q_{m}])$, and $\mathbf p_\ell= 0$ on $[\mathbf Q_{\ell-1}, \mathbf Q_m]$;
    \item for each $j\in \llbracket m+1, m+\mathbf u\rrbracket$, $\mathbf p_j \in \mathfrak B([0,\mathbf Q_m])$ and $\mathbf p_j$ is not identical zero.
    \item for each $j\in \llbracket 1, m+\mathbf u\rrbracket$, $\ell \in \llbracket 1, m\rrbracket$, $\mathbf p_j$ is left-continuous at $x=\mathbf Q_{\ell-1}$ unless $j=\ell$.
    \item regularity condition spelled in Definition (defn:blp of the paper) below.\footnote{Here is some intuition for the definition of a block process. It corresponds to the degrees of polynomials in Dunkl operators expansion, as shown later in (sec:gme of the paper). The values of $\mathbf p_\ell$ at points $[0,\mathbf Q_{\ell-1}]$ for $\ell \in \llbracket 1, m\rrbracket$ relate to the degrees of variables $x_i$ with indices matching one of the Dunkl operators $\mathfrak D_i^N$ (to be introduced in (sec:dunkl of the paper)) we are expanding, and $\mathbf p_j$ for $j\in\llbracket m+1, m+\mathbf u\rrbracket$ are the degrees of the other variables. In particular, the variable corresponding to the first operator would have zero degree after $\mathbf Q_0=0$, so $\mathbf p_1$ is identical zero.}
\end{itemize}

