[Defn def:tree of arXiv:2601.00119, 'The largest common subtree of two random trees'] A \emph{plane tree} is a (potentially infinite) subset $t$ of $\mathcal{U}$ satisfying the following conditions:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item[(a)] $\varnothing\in t$,
    \item[(b)] for all $u\in t$, if $u\neq\varnothing$ then $\overleftarrow{u}\in t$,
    \item[(c)] for all $u\in t$, there is an integer $\mathrm{k}_u(t)\geq 0$ such that $u * (i)\in t \Leftrightarrow 1\leq i\leq  \mathrm{k}_u(t)$ for all $i \in \mathbb{N}^*$.
\end{enumerate}

