[Lemma lem:second-summand of arXiv:2412.09145, 'Asymptotic expansions for normal deviations of random walks conditioned to stay positive'] Under the conditions of Theorem (thm:lattice of the paper) it holds, with $z=x/\sigma$,
\begin{multline*}
    \sum_{y\le|x|/4} 
            \mathbf P(X = -y)\mathbf P(S_{n-1} = x+y)
=
    e^{-\frac{z^2}{2n}}
    \sum_{\nu=1}^{r+1}
        \frac{P_{\nu}^{(2)}\big(z/\sqrt{n}\big)}{n^{\nu/2}}
\\
+
    O\left(\frac{1}{(\min(\sqrt{n},|x|))^{r+2}}\right).
\end{multline*}
where $P_\nu^{(2)}$ are some polynomials.

