body:
[Theorem dimhatleastconjecture of arXiv:2506.10448, 'Hitting probabilities and the Ekstr\"om--Persson conjecture'] For every $\mu \in \mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^d)$ {and} for every $\alpha>0$, one has 
\begin{equation}
\overline{F}_{\mu}\Bigl(\frac 1\alpha\Bigr) \leq f_{\mu}(\alpha)\leq \min\Bigl\{
  \frac{1}{\alpha}, \overline{H}_{\mu}\Bigl(\frac 1\alpha\Bigr)\Bigr\},
\end{equation}
and the above bounds are optimal. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem 5 (Sampling Theorem) of arXiv:2609.03418, 'Sampling and Density Theorems for the Fractional Opdam--Cherednik Transform'] Let $ f\in PW^\theta_{\alpha,\beta}.$
Then
\begin{align}
f(\lambda) = f(0)S_0^\theta(\lambda) + \sum_{j\in\mathbb Z\setminus\{0\}} f(s_j)S_j^\theta(\lambda),
\end{align}
where
\begin{align}
S_0^\theta(\lambda) = e^{-\frac i2\lambda^2\cot\theta} \frac{ \Psi_{\alpha,\beta}(\lambda\csc\theta) }{ \Psi_{\alpha,\beta}(0) }, 
\end{align}
and, for $j\ne0$,
\begin{align}
S_j^\theta(\lambda) = e^{-\frac i2(\lambda^2-s_j^2)\cot\theta} \frac{ \lambda\sin\theta }{ s_j(\lambda-s_j) } \frac{ \Psi_{\alpha,\beta}(\lambda\csc\theta) }{ \Psi_{\alpha,\beta}'(\mu_j) }, \quad \mu_j=s_j\csc\theta. 
\end{align}
The value at $\lambda=s_j$ in \eqref{Sec4_Eqn18} is understood by continuity. The interpolation functions satisfy
\begin{align}
S_j^\theta(s_k)=\delta_{jk}, \quad j,k\in\mathbb Z.
\end{align}
The series in \eqref{Sec4_Eqn16} converges in the $PW^\theta_{\alpha,\beta}$-norm and uniformly on compact subsets of $\mathbb R$.

