[Prop 23 of arXiv:2605.21638, 'Markov renewal theory for transfer operators and point processes on the line'] For all $x_0<0$ and bounded, local measurable $F\colon \mathbf{N} \rightarrow \R$, we have 
    \begin{equation*}
        \lim_{n\rightarrow\infty} \int_{\R^n} F(\delta_{x_0} + \dots + \delta_{x_n}) \dd \mu_{n,\beta}^{x_0} = \E_{\zeta}[F(\Theta_{x_0}\Phi^+ )],
    \end{equation*}
    where $\P_{\zeta}$ denote the distribution of the Markov chain $(Z_n)_{n\geq 0}$ with $Z_0 \sim \zeta$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

