[Lemma lem:technical_lemma_integrability of arXiv:2602.19773, 'Regularization of a stationary point process by a stationary increments perturbation'] Let $\xi$ be a stationary and ergodic point process with finite intensity $\lambda_{\xi}$. Then, 
		\begin{equation*}
			\lim_{\sigma \to +\infty}\frac{1}{\sigma^{d}}\@ifnextchar[{\@withe}{\@withoute}{\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}f\left(\frac{x}{\sigma}\right) \, \hat{\xi}(\mathrm{d}x)} = \lambda_{\xi}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}} f(x)\, \mathrm{d}x.
		\end{equation*}
		for any continuous and integrable $f : \mathbb{R}^{d}\longrightarrow \mathbb{R}$.

