[Theorem 6 of arXiv:2608.26662, 'Boundary–Moment Universality and Curvature Corrections in Random Geometric Graphs on Riema'] Under the standing assumptions, assume $d>6$ and define
$r_{2,n}(t):=t n^{-3/(2d)}$.
Then, as $n\to\infty$, for every $T<\infty$, uniformly for
$0\le t\le T$,
\[
\begin{aligned}
\log\Pp\{S_{2,n}>r_{2,n}(t)\}
={}&-A_2(d)t^{2d}\int_M f^3\,d\mathrm{vol}_g\\
&+C_2(d)t^{2d+2}n^{-3/d}
\left\{
\begin{aligned}
&\int_M f\|\grad f\|_g^2\,d\mathrm{vol}_g\\
&+\frac16\int_M f^3\Scal_g\,d\mathrm{vol}_g
\end{aligned}
\right\}
+o(n^{-3/d}).
\end{aligned}
\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition prop:uniform_contraction of arXiv:2606.05377, 'The Clark-Kushner condition for interacting reinforced random walks on finite graphs'] Under Assumptions~(ass:H1 of the paper)--(ass:H2 of the paper), there exist constants $C^* > 0$, $\lambda \in (0,1)$, and an integer $k_* \geq 1$ such that for all $x \in \triangle$ and $k \geq 0$:
\begin{equation}
\|Q(x)^k - \Pi(x)\| \leq C^* \lambda^k.
\end{equation}

[Lemma lem:weighted-bias of arXiv:2607.19583, 'Density-Dependent McKean--Vlasov Diffusions: Subgaussian Occupancy Bounds and Polynomial P'] Under Assumptions~(ass:coefficients of the paper) and (ass:density of the paper), the cell averages inherit Gaussian decay $\Pi_{h,U}p_t(x) \le C e^{-c'|x|^2}$, and the deterministic bias 
\begin{equation}
\beta_h(t) := \sup_{x\in\mathbb R^d} |\nabla\Phi(x)|^2 |\Xi(\mathsf R_{h,L} p_t(x))-\Xi(p_t(x))|^2
\end{equation}
satisfies $\beta_h(t) \le C_T \min\{1,h^2/t\}$ uniformly across shifts. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

