[Prop 3 of arXiv:2609.00739, '2609.00739'] Under the hypotheses of Theorem~\ref{thm:main}, a subsequence satisfies
the following preliminary conclusions:
\begin{enumerate}[label=$(\theenumi)$]
\item there is a finite-perimeter partition $(E_a)_{a=1}^q$ such that
\[
 u_j\to\sum_{a=1}^q\upsigma_a\mathbf1_{E_a}
 \quad\text{in }L^1(\Omega);
\]
\item the measures $\upnu_j$, $\upzeta_j$, and $\upmu_{j,ab}$ converge weakly
star on $\overline\Omega$ to Radon measures $\nustar$, $\zetastar$, and
finite signed Radon measures $\upmu_{\star,ab}$;
\item on every $U\subset\subset\Omega$, the limits have the interior properties
stated in Theorem~\ref{thm:bethuel-interior};
\item for every $X\in C^1(\overline\Omega;\R^2)$ tangent to
$\partial\Omega$,
\begin{equation}
 \int_{\overline\Omega}\diver X\dd\nustar
 -\int_{\overline\Omega}\partial_iX_j\dd\upmu_{\star,ij}=0.
\end{equation}
\end{enumerate}

