{"artifact_digest":"sha256:053cf7f8b673eae06001428752216c8a61737017e0fe06d2c3b41fa6ace32a44","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/05/053cf7f8b673eae06001428752216c8a61737017e0fe06d2c3b41fa6ace32a44.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:c60b4584ed6cc3b95885d29161924850f373a724ec6566ea2eb824ee13b22711","bundle_entry_key":"kruskal-sublevel-intrinsic-diameter-lower-transfer","bundle_id":"population.w344-open-problem-c0087-checked-partials-20261010","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"w344/bundle_007.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:probability.minimum_spanning_trees:kruskal-sublevel-intrinsic-diameter-lower-transfer","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Open Problem 16.3 in the same cached source asks for MST diameter of order V^(1/3) on high-dimensional tori and the hypercube. The prior proposed reduction lacked complete geometric hypotheses. We prove only its deterministic lower-bound step.

Let G be a finite connected graph with distinct edge weights, T its MST, and G_p the graph of edges with weight <=p. Kruskal's algorithm has, by level p, selected a spanning tree inside every component C of G_p. These selected edges remain in T. Hence the unique T path between any u,v in C lies inside C, and its length is at least their shortest-path distance in C. Consequently max_C diam_intrinsic(C)<=diam(T). Any probabilistic lower bound for the left side transfers directly to the MST diameter without a universality assumption.

The reverse inequality fails: on K_n give the edges of a Hamilton path the n-1 smallest weights and every other edge larger distinct weights. Kruskal selects exactly that path, so diam(T)=n-1. At a threshold including every edge, G_p=K_n has intrinsic diameter 1. Thus intrinsic cluster-diameter control at one level gives no MST upper bound. This does not refute high-dimensional scaling. The script checks all 38 connected labeled four-vertex graphs at every selected threshold and exact K_4,K_8,K_16 path examples. Full torus/hypercube bounds remain unresolved in this packet.","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:ded8fddb33a606a358455f809c33b51023b9de4319e7cfbdbc3fdfbe6e6a4a4b","revision_digest":"sha256:ff2c306f2aacf69a54d5699409acc2e8b7a73e6493942f300116f1003df99af2","source_id":"owner-w344-open-problems-20261010:kruskal-sublevel-intrinsic-diameter-lower-transfer","source_revision":"2026-10-10 worker result; proof; independent audit pending w346; novelty unverified","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

