[Prop Sigma-bullet-homotopical-left-Quillen of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] Let $G$ be compact Lie. The adjunctions
    \begin{align*}
        \Sigma^\bullet_+\colon\cat{$\bm G$-$\textbf{\textup{L}}$-Top}&\rightleftarrows\cat{$\bm{G}$-OrthSp}
	\nobreak
	\mspace{6mu plus 1mu}
	{:}
	\nonscript\mkern-\thinmuskip
	\mathpunct{}
	\mspace{2mu}
\Omega^\bullet\\
        \Sigma^\bullet\colon\cat{$\bm G$-$\textbf{\textup{L}}$-Top}_*&\rightleftarrows\cat{$\bm{G}$-OrthSp}
	\nobreak
	\mspace{6mu plus 1mu}
	{:}
	\nonscript\mkern-\thinmuskip
	\mathpunct{}
	\mspace{2mu}
\Omega^\bullet
    \end{align*}
    are Quillen adjunctions, and $\Sigma^\bullet_+$ is fully homotopical.
    \begin{proof}
        It is clear from the definition that $\Omega^\bullet$ preserves fibrant objects, i.e.\ it sends $G$-global $\Omega$-spectra to static $G$-orthogonal spaces. To complete the proof that these are Quillen adjunctions, it will then suffice by [HTT]*{Corollary A.3.7.2} that $\Sigma^\bullet$ preserves cofibrations or, equivalently, that $\Omega^\bullet$ preserves acyclic (level) fibrations as a functor to $\cat{$\bm G$-$\textbf{\textup{L}}$-Top}_*$. Plugging in the definitions, this amounts to saying that
        \[
            S^V\smashp{-}\colon\cat{$\bm{({\textup{O}}(V)\times G)}$-Top}_*\rightleftarrows\cat{$\bm{({\textup{O}}(V)\times G)}$-Top}_*
	\nobreak
	\mspace{6mu plus 1mu}
	{:}
	\nonscript\mkern-\thinmuskip
	\mathpunct{}
	\mspace{2mu}
\Omega^V
        \] 
        is a Quillen adjunction for the $\mathcal G_{{\textup{O}}(V),G}$-model structure. This is an instance of Lemma~(lemma:smash-lQ of the paper), using  that $S^V$ admits the structure of an $({\textup{O}}(V)\times G)$-CW-complex.

        It remains to show that $\Sigma^\bullet_+$ is homotopical, for which it will suffice by factoring a general weak equivalence into an acyclic cofibration followed by an acyclic fibration that $\Sigma^\bullet_+$ preserves $G$-global level weak equivalences. Plugging in the definitions this amounts to saying that
        \[
            S^V\smashp (-)_+\colon\cat{$\bm{({\textup{O}}(V)\times G)}$-Top}\to\cat{$\bm{({\textup{O}}(V)\times G)}$-Top}_*
        \]
        preserves $\mathcal G_{{\textup{O}}(V),G}$-weak equivalences, which is an instance of Proposition~(prop:smash-well-based of the paper).
    \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Thm 2 of arXiv:2510.21595, 'One-arm exponents of high-dimensional percolation revisited'] Let $d>6$. Let $L_0$ be given by Theorem \textup{\ref{thm: main result}}, and $L\geq L_0$. There exist $c,C>0$ such that, for $n\geq 1$,
	\begin{equation}
		\frac{c}{n^3} 
		\leq  \P_{p_c}[0\connect{\mathbb H\:}\Lambda_{n}^c]   \leq \frac{C}{n^3}.
	\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 14 of arXiv:2607.14718, 'Anchored Nash inequalities and heat kernel bounds for a class of random conductance models'] For any $a, b > 0$ and any $\alpha > 1$,

  \begin{align*}
    \bigl(a^{1+\alpha} - b^{1+\alpha}\bigr)
    \bigl(a^{1-\alpha} - b^{1-\alpha}\bigr)
    \;\geq\;
    (a - b)^{2} - \alpha^{2} a^{1-\alpha} b^{1-\alpha}
    \biggl(
      \frac{a^{\alpha-1} + b^{\alpha-1}}{2}
    \biggr)^{2} (a-b)^{2}.
  \end{align*}

