body:
[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2608.01516, 'Nondegeneracy and regularity of polynomial pushforwards'] Let $\alpha\in(0,1]$ and let $\nu$ be a probability Borel measure on $\mathbb R^k$.
Then the estimate
\begin{equation}
\nu(A)\le C\bigl(\lambda_k(A)\bigr)^\alpha
\end{equation}
for every Borel set $A\subset \mathbb R^k$ is equivalent to the estimate
\begin{equation}
\int_{\mathbb R^k}\psi\,d\nu\le C\|\psi\|_{L^1(\mathbb R^k)}^\alpha
\end{equation}
for every $\psi\in C_0^\infty(\mathbb R^k)$ with $0\le\psi\le 1$.

