body:
[Lemma CLTSmin of arXiv:2606.09386, 'High-degree vertices in uniform recursive directed acyclic graphs with freezing'] Consider the same notation and conditions as in Proposition~(prop:depthlabelsinglevertex of the paper). Additionally, recall $\mathcal{S}_n^-(a_1)$ from~(equation eq:definition_selection_sets_ungreedy_depth_single_vertex of the paper) and let $\text{Geo}_m\sim \mathrm{Geo}(1/(m+1))$ be independent of $\mathcal{S}_n^-(a_1)$. Fix $y\in \mathbb{R}$ and define the event 
\begin{equation} 
\mathcal{E}_n(d,y)\coloneq \{|\mathcal{S}_n^-(a_1)\cap [L(d,y),n]|\geq d+\text{Geo}_m\}. 
\end{equation} 
Then, 
\begin{equation} 
\lim_{n\to\infty}\mathbb{P}\!\left(\mathcal{E}_n(d,y)\right)=1-\Phi(y),
\end{equation}
where $\Phi$ denotes the cumulative density function of the standard normal distribution.

